            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0463" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93/121: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-29T16:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 29—9:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>11. Secretary’s statement on Chinese policy well received here by Japanese press
                    which feels that in general it coincides with Japanese Government’s policy.
                    Although I have not discussed statement with Foreign Office, I understand from
                    colleague who has talked with Vice Minister that they are pleased with stand we
                    have taken.</p>
                <p>Full text not being available here I have asked Peking to forward copy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
